    "summary": "Explosive Dark Star > Sugar Magnolia > Caution with tight jams",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a blistering Dark Star‑to‑Sugar Magnolia‑to‑Caution sequence and strong performances of Good Lovin' and Mr. Charlie. Pigpen’s organ adds high‑octane color while Jerry and Phil drive the improvisations. The crystal‑clear Miller soundboard capture makes this one of the standout Europe ’72 dates.",
    "review": "April 29, 1972 at Hamburg's Musikhalle finds the Dead in top form, rolling out a two‑set marathon that balances soulful blues with soaring psychedelia. The first set builds momentum with tight renditions of Good Lovin', Big Boss Man and a gritty Mr. Charlie, while Pigpen’s organ roars on tracks like China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider. The second half erupts into the show's centerpiece: a sprawling Dark Star that morphs seamlessly into an exuberant Sugar Magnolia and detonates in a thunderous Caution (Do Not Stop On Tracks). Jerry’s tone is razor‑sharp, Phil’s bass drives the improvisations forward, and Keith’s piano adds crystalline depth. Bill Kreutzmann lays down a solid groove that holds the high‑energy flow together, making this performance one of the most compelling snapshots of the Europe ’72 tour.",
